  "Railgun: 150 damage in file and registry, no falloff effect (150 at both ends, 100 to 200 m), 1029 m/s, one round per magazine with 11 magazines, reload 4.266 s. Against a tank the product is 375 before the hit factor (281 turret, 375 body, 563 side, 750 rear by L3323's factors); 525 against helicopters and jets; 825 against light vehicles. A soldier takes 150 on any body part by the scalar (the array is present but empty), above 100 health.",
  "Panzerfaust 3: direct damage 100 on material 125, the RPG's material, so 200 against tanks before the hit factor (150 to 400), 900 against helicopters, 1000 against jets; blast 130 with grid 1.0 against soldiers and 0 against armour. The DM32 rocket has direct 100 on another material and blast 230.",
  "The Panzerfaust figures are file-only values: no registry row exists, and L3343 showed such values can be stale. The RPG's own registry damage is 125 on the same material, which would make the Panzerfaust the weaker of the two against tanks if 100 is current.",
  "Whether either weapon is obtainable in the current multiplayer modes is not read from these files."
 ],
